VI editor has three modes of operations.
  Command Mode
  Insert Mode
  Ex Mode (Extended Command Mode)

To Go to Insert mode from command mode
  i   		-  Inserts the text at the current cursor position
  I   		-  Inserts the text in beginning of a line
  a  		-  Adds the text after the current cursor position 
  A  		-  Adds the text at the end of a line
  o 		-  Inserts the text one line below current cursor position
  O 		-  Inserts the text one line above current cursor position

EX mode
  :q		-  Quit without saving 
  :q!   		-  Quit forcefully without saving 
  :w  		-  Write (save)
  :wq  		-  write and quit
  :wq!		-  Write and quit forcefully 
  :se nu	-  Sets line numbers 
  :se nonu	-  Removes line numbers 
  :84  		-  The cursor goes to line 84
  1,$s/old name/new name  - Replace the word name

Command Mode
  dd   			-  Deletes a line
  ndd   		-  Deletes ‘n’ lines
  yy  			-  Copies a line
  nyy  			-  Copies ‘n’ lines
  p		 	 -  Put (pastes the deleted or copied text)
  u			 -  Undo (you can undo 1000 times)
  Ctrl+r		 -  Redo
  G			 - Moves the cursor to the last line of the file
  /<word to find>	-  Finds a word (press n for next)

To create a file using vi
  syn: vi <filename>
  eg: #vi m1
  To create a file using vim
  syn: vim <filename>
  eg: #vim m2
  To Create or open multiple files
  syn: vim -o <filename> <filename>
  eg: #vim -o m1 m2

Advantages of VIM
  1. using vim we can open multiple files at a time:
  syn:vim -o <filename> <filename>
  eg: #vim -o f1 f2
  To switch files
  ctrl+ww

  2.We can check content of configuration files in colors
    syn: vim <configuration file>
    eg: #vim /etc/passwd

3.We can encrypt a file by assigning password
  X is used to assign password
  change password and remove password from extended mode.
    example
    To assign password
    #vim myfile
    :X
    New Encryption Key:xxxx
    Retype same Encryption key:xxxx
    Esc:wq
    Verify:
    #cat myfile

  To change password
    #vim myfile
    Encryption key:xxxx
    :X
    New Encryption Key:xxxxx
    Retpe same Encrytption Key:xxxxxx
    Esc:wq
    Verify:
    #cat myfile
  To Remove Password
    #vim myfile
    Encryption key:xxxxxx
    :X
    New Encryption Key:(Press Enter button)
    Retype EncryptionKey:Press enter
    Esc:wq
    To Verify:
    #cat myfile
    #vim myfile